{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-265712",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The first term is ${a}_{1}=1,$ and the common ratio is $r=-2,$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $6$th term, we can use this formula with $n=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =1\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{6} & =1\\cdot (-2)^{6-1} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)^{5} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-32) \\\\  & =-32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $6$th term is ${a}_{6}=-32.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
